# WanderSync — Agent Guide

## What This Is

WanderSync is a group travel planning app being built for HackDuke: Code for Good 2026 (Interactive Media track). Users paste travel links → AI extracts locations → group members vote via pairwise comparison → app generates an optimized day itinerary → users follow it in real-time → when plans break, the app replans automatically.

The `/src/app/components/` directory contains **Figma Make-generated TSX components** — these are the visual source of truth for every screen. Transform these presentational components into a fully functional application with real state management, routing, and animations.

## Current State

- Vite dev server with React 18 + React Router 7
- All screens in `src/app/components/*.tsx` as presentational components
- Navigation via `useState<Screen>` in `src/app/App.tsx` — must migrate to React Router
- No state management — all data is hardcoded inline
- No API layer, no shared types file, no store
- Tailwind CSS 4 with shadcn/radix primitives in `src/app/components/ui/`
- Framer Motion already installed as the `motion` package

## Target Stack — DO NOT migrate to Next.js. Keep Vite + React Router.

| Layer       | Technology                                         |
|-------------|----------------------------------------------------|
| Bundler     | Vite (keep existing `vite.config.ts`)              |
| Framework   | React 18 + React Router 7                         |
| Styling     | Tailwind CSS 4                                     |
| State       | Zustand                                            |
| Animations  | Framer Motion (import from `motion/react`)         |
| Maps        | Mapbox GL JS or Google Maps                        |
| AI/LLM      | Anthropic SDK (`claude-sonnet-4-20250514`) via proxy |
| Fonts       | DM Serif Display (headings), DM Sans (body), JetBrains Mono (data) |

## Route Structure (React Router)

All routes defined in `src/app/App.tsx` using `<Routes>`:

```
/                            → Trip Home (screen 1)
/trip/:id/import             → Import Content (screen 2)
/trip/:id/vote               → Pairwise Comparison (screen 3)
/trip/:id/results            → Group Results (screen 4)
/trip/:id/preferences        → Trip Preferences (screen 5)
/trip/:id/plan               → Day Itinerary + Map (screen 6)
/trip/:id/live               → Execution Mode (screen 7)
```

SalvageModal is an overlay on `/trip/:id/live`, not its own route.

