## API Strategy

For the hackathon demo, LLM calls are handled client-side with hardcoded fallbacks:

1. **Primary**: Hardcoded fallback responses in `/lib/api.ts` — no API key needed, demo always works
2. **Stretch**: Vite dev server proxy to Anthropic API via `vite.config.ts` → `server.proxy`

## Build Priority

1. Types + seed data + Zustand store (foundation)
2. React Router setup in App.tsx (replace useState navigation)
3. Pairwise voting with Elo (core differentiator)
4. Execution mode with countdown timer
5. Salvage mode with replan animation
6. Itinerary generation (hardcoded fallback OK)
7. Map integration, URL import, trip creation (nice-to-have)

## Key Constraints

- Mobile-first: 390×844 viewport, 44px minimum touch targets
- All LLM features MUST have hardcoded fallbacks so the demo works without API keys
- Seed data: 15 Tokyo activities with real coordinates
- Demo must work end-to-end with seed data alone
- Preserve original Figma component files as visual reference — create new files in `/src/pages/` and `/src/components/`
